A web is in the form of a grid with $100 \times 100$ nodes (in other words, this is a grid with $99 \times 99$ cells). A spider sits in one corner, and flies are stuck to the web at some 100 nodes. In one move, the spider can move to any adjacent node. Can the spider guarantee to eat all the flies in no more than 

a) 2100 moves;
b) 2000 moves?

Find the $\operatorname{rot} \dot{A}$ if:

a) $\dot{A}=\frac{y}{z} \dot{i}+\frac{z}{x} \dot{j}+\frac{x}{y} \dot{k}$;

b) $\dot{A}=r \dot{i} f(r)$, where $f(r)$ is an arbitrary differentiable function $\left(r=\sqrt{x^{2}+y^{2}+z^{2}}\right)$.

In a chess tournament, each participant played exactly once with each of the others, and there were no draws. Prove that there exists a player \( P \) such that, for any other player \( Q \), distinct from \( P \), one of the following situations occurs:
i) \( Q \) lost to \( P \);

ii) \( Q \) lost to someone who lost to \( P \).

Marcos wants to weigh a banana, an apple, and a papaya on a two-pan balance scale. In each of the given figures, the scale is balanced, meaning the contents on the right pan have the same weight as those on the left pan. In two of the three weighings, a weight of 200 grams was used. We can state that the total weight of the three fruits, in grams, is

(a) 250 ;
(b) 300 ;
(c) 350 ;
(d) 400 ;
(e) 450 .

Prove that there exist sequences of natural numbers \( a_{n} \) and \( b_{n} \) such that the following conditions are simultaneously satisfied:

- The sequences \( a_{n} \) and \( b_{n} \) are non-decreasing;
- The sequences \( A_{n}=\frac{1}{a_{1}}+\frac{1}{a_{2}}+\ldots+\frac{1}{a_{n}} \) and \( B_{n}=\frac{1}{b_{1}}+\frac{1}{b_{2}}+\ldots+\frac{1}{b_{n}} \) are unbounded;
- The sequence \( C_{n}=\frac{1}{\max \left(a_{1}, b_{1}\right)}+\frac{1}{\max \left(a_{2}, b_{2}\right)}+\ldots+\frac{1}{\max \left(a_{n}, b_{n}\right)} \) is bounded.

Given that \(a\), \(b\), and \(c\) are positive numbers. Prove the inequality:
$$
\begin{array}{l}
\sqrt{a^{2}+a b+b^{2}}+\sqrt{a^{2}+a c+c^{2}} \\
\geqslant 4 \sqrt{\left(\frac{a b}{a+b}\right)^{2}+\left(\frac{a b}{a+b}\right)\left(\frac{a c}{a+c}\right)+\left(\frac{a c}{a+c}\right)^{2}}
\end{array}
$$
